1
00:00:00,790 --> 00:00:03,040
-[footsteps]
-[Xylo panting]

2
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:07,630
♪

3
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:14,060
[TEORITTA] Wait, my knight.

4
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,730
This is not the path
that we initially took.

5
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,890
We already have our next orders.

6
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:19,940
[Venetim sighs]

7
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:23,480
[XYLO] There's no
one set path for heroes.

8
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:26,610
-[birds chirping]
-[ducks quacking]

9
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:29,530
[horse neighs]

10
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:34,160
There are many more
travelers here.

11
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,330
[VENETIM] We're all
off to the same place,

12
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:39,540
which is holding
something of a festival.

13
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,000
-Quick question, Xylo.
-[XYLO] What?

14
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:45,420
[panting] I'm about to die.

15
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:48,720
Can we take a break
sooner than later?

16
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,260
We had one a minute ago.

17
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,800
[VENETIM] I can't go on.

18
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:55,010
[thuds]

19
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:03,190
Uh, is that our
next destination?

20
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:04,400
Correct.

21
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:07,030
It's a fortress
of the Second Capital.

22
00:01:07,070 --> 00:01:09,190
A key part of their defenses.

23
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:11,660
[XYLO]
A natural stronghold

24
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:14,410
guarded by a river
and sheer cliffs.

25
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,870
[XYLO] That's Mureed Fortress.

26
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:20,660
Otherwise known
as the Wayfarer's Nest.

27
00:01:20,710 --> 00:01:23,000
♪

28
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:26,880
[MERCHANT 1]
Lowest prices around!

29
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,460
[indistinct chatter]

30
00:01:29,510 --> 00:01:30,930
♪

31
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,260
[merchant 2 chuckles]
Whoops,

32
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,930
seems you need
more military scrip.

33
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:36,890
I'll take five of these.

34
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:39,730
[POSTMAN] Does anyone here
have a letter to send out?

35
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,730
Send anywhere

36
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:42,350
-in the Federated Kingdom.
-Take these to my mother.

37
00:01:42,390 --> 00:01:43,600
[POSTMAN] No problem!

38
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:46,900
[sighs]

39
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,190
[VENETIM] Fresh from repairs

40
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:51,030
and already back
to your old tricks.

41
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,450
You're incorrigible, Dotta.

42
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:55,410
Relax, will you?

43
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:56,660
No one's gonna get mad

44
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:59,040
over some harmless pilfering
at a festival.

45
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:01,750
We haven't attended
the Great Exchange in a while,

46
00:02:01,790 --> 00:02:03,500
but don't go getting careless.

47
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:06,790
The Verkle Corp merchants
are notoriously miserly.

48
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:09,050
[exclaims]

49
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:11,630
I say we should enjoy
this while we can.

50
00:02:11,670 --> 00:02:14,640
It's not often
we get to have a vacation.

51
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:18,680
Heroes like us aren't allowed
the luxury of a vacation.

52
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:19,970
Even as of now,

53
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:22,390
we're "on standby."

54
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:25,560
But that said, technically,

55
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,570
we're not disallowed
the occasional respite.

56
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,820
[Dotta sighs]

57
00:02:31,030 --> 00:02:32,280
[DOTTA] That's what I said

58
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:35,490
just rephrased to make yourself
sound smarter.

59
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:43,200
[DOTTA] All we're missing is
some girls to keep us company.

60
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:44,750
[VENETIM] You're dreaming.

61
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:47,170
Even if there were
such an establishment here,

62
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:49,960
we'd never be allowed
to partake.

63
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,250
[DOTTA] No kidding.

64
00:02:54,130 --> 00:02:56,840
[NORGALLE] Commander-in-chief,
where are you?

65
00:02:56,890 --> 00:02:59,600
-Commander Xylo!
-[XYLO] Huh?

66
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:01,140
At attention,

67
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,390
the traveling merchants
have arrived.

68
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:05,520
Your king needs you
to procure some wine!

69
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,110
I'm afraid our treasury
is fairly depleted

70
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:09,440
for the time being.

71
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,780
Guessing you forgot
spending all of our scrip?

72
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:12,820
[Norgalle gasps]

73
00:03:12,990 --> 00:03:14,360
If you want booze,

74
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,660
then you'll have to get
someone to take out a loan.

75
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,490
Someone like Venetim.

76
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:20,200
[NORGALLE] The chancellor
is keeping an eye

77
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,410
on that sticky-fingered Dotta.

78
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:24,660
Always has a fresh excuse
to slack off.

79
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:26,460
What of Tsav?
Has he not returned

80
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,920
from his mission yet?

81
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:31,050
[XYLO] No. He's still out
on loan to another unit.

82
00:03:31,090 --> 00:03:33,670
[grunts]
Flagrant insubordination!

83
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:35,590
Does the crown mean
nothing anymore?

84
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:37,840
Honestly, it seems
a moment of peace

85
00:03:37,890 --> 00:03:39,800
-is too much to ask.
-[panting]

86
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:43,310
There you are!

87
00:03:43,350 --> 00:03:45,430
I have been searching
high and low!

88
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:47,600
-[lock rattling]
-[XYLO] Confirms my theory.

89
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:49,690
-[door opens]
-Your chamber door's unlocked.

90
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:52,020
Does that not defeat
its very purpose?

91
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:54,530
Dotta unlocked it
and scampered away.

92
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:56,320
He took the key with him.

93
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,950
Do you not wish to attend
the Great Exchange, my knight?

94
00:03:58,990 --> 00:04:00,950
I don't wanna talk
to any damn knights.

95
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:03,700
Then come and make merry
with me instead!

96
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:05,500
I have no reason to.

97
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:07,620
Just go to the Great Exchange
yourself.

98
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:11,130
[gasps] Need I remind you that
you are addressing a goddess?

99
00:04:11,170 --> 00:04:13,800
I have no interest
in such frivolity.

100
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,050
[Xylo scoffs]

101
00:04:15,090 --> 00:04:17,510
A Holy Knight would be
happy to escort you.

102
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:18,630
[Teoritta grunts]

103
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:21,010
Let us speak no more
of the Exchange.

104
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:22,220
Instead,

105
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:25,600
I shall now grant you the honor
of playing a game with me!

106
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,430
Are you not elated?

107
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,770
[XYLO] Zig?

108
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:31,810
Venetim took it upon himself
to teach me all the rules.

109
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:34,320
I shall prove
a formidable opponent.

110
00:04:34,690 --> 00:04:35,860
[Teoritta chuckles]

111
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:36,940
The trick is to use

112
00:04:36,990 --> 00:04:38,780
the venerable
"hidden spear" strategy

113
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:41,450
oft utilized by the royal family
in the Kingdom of Meht.

114
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:42,820
That's enough.

115
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:46,700
If Venetim taught you that,
he was messing with you.

116
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:48,000
[gasps]

117
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,290
[Xylo sighs]

118
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:51,880
And besides,
I've already got plans.

119
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,840
What? Do you speak of that book?

120
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:55,710
Can you not study it
some other time?

121
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:58,260
Look, I even made
a bookmark for you.

122
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,590
I don't care, you can keep it.

123
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:01,890
♪

124
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,180
[TEORITTA] I must admit,

125
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,140
it is surprising
that you love reading so.

126
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,230
What manner of text
is that you're--

127
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:10,270
[XYLO] It's poetry.

128
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,100
Is that true?

129
00:05:12,150 --> 00:05:13,190
♪

130
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:16,480
[TEORITTA]
My knight reads poetry?

131
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:18,530
[XYLO] Sure, why wouldn't I?

132
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,610
What manner of verse is it?

133
00:05:20,650 --> 00:05:23,570
I shall allow you the privilege
of reading it to me, now.

134
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:25,490
-Denied.
-[grunts]

135
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:28,450
At the least, permit me
to read over your shoulder.

136
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,910
Do not be cruel.

137
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:32,870
[sighs] I don't think
a goddess would get anything

138
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,210
out of this book.

139
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:35,840
It's just a collection

140
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:38,340
of old poems
called Dragon-Drunk.

141
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:42,300
Written by an alcoholic poet
by the name of Altoyard Comette.

142
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:45,180
In his old age, he dreamed
of becoming a dragon,

143
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:48,850
and practiced flying every night
until it led to his demise.

144
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:50,310
[TEORITTA] Oh...

145
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:52,310
Quite the fantastical tale.

146
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:55,520
[XYLO] There were a lot of poets
like him in those days.

147
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,650
I might have become
a poet myself

148
00:05:57,690 --> 00:05:59,730
if I hadn't joined the military.

149
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:00,940
A poet?

150
00:06:00,990 --> 00:06:03,030
What of it? Why is that so--

151
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,910
-[KIVIA] Xylo Forbartz.
-[TEORITTA] Huh?

152
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:06,780
Finally found you.

153
00:06:07,030 --> 00:06:09,830
Though I didn't expect
to also find the goddess.

154
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:12,830
Greetings, Kivia, I deem it
a most pleasant surprise

155
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:14,330
to see you here as well!

156
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:15,500
[Xylo chuckles]

157
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:17,960
So the noble captain
of the Holy Knights

158
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,880
has deigned to pay me a visit.

159
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:23,010
I take it our punishment
has been decided?

160
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:26,050
Either that, or a new mission.

161
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:28,350
You're correct on both counts.

162
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:31,060
Regardless,
that isn't why I'm here.

163
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:33,190
I need to have a word with you.

164
00:06:33,230 --> 00:06:34,560
What about?

165
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,650
Follow me. I'll unlock--

166
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:39,400
[TEORITTA] I shall join you.

167
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,610
[XYLO] Huh?

168
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:41,990
[TEORITTA]
I have been informed

169
00:06:42,030 --> 00:06:43,820
that the Great Exchange
is underway.

170
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:46,570
It seems fitting that we should
speak as we browse about.

171
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:49,030
With Kivia present,
even a goddess like me

172
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:51,080
will surely be
allowed to attend.

173
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,790
Indeed, truly, it must be so.

174
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:56,380
My knight,
I demand we make haste.

175
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:57,830
Fine.

176
00:06:58,460 --> 00:06:59,750
♪

177
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:01,880
[indistinct chatter]

178
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:06,630
[Teoritta humming, chuckling]

179
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:10,890
-Really?
-[TEORITTA] Xylo, behold!

180
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:12,970
What is that over yonder?

181
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:15,270
Nourishment or
a decoration of some sort?

182
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:18,310
[XYLO] That's candy.
First time seeing it?

183
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,480
[TEORITTA] "Can-dy"?

184
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:23,860
This marvel did not yet exist
in the time I was created.

185
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:26,570
They are rather reminiscent
of shining jewels.

186
00:07:26,610 --> 00:07:28,660
[gasps, sniffs]

187
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:32,330
-What is that long, thin stuff?
-[XYLO] Uh?

188
00:07:32,370 --> 00:07:33,700
Fried noodles.

189
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:36,370
A western dish
of wheat-dough strips fried

190
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:38,250
in butter and fermented sauce.

191
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:39,540
How delightful!

192
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:41,130
And what are those things?

193
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:43,840
There, at the stall
with the bear sign.

194
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:45,590
[XYLO] That would be...

195
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:47,720
The hell? I'm not sure.

196
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:49,510
[KIVIA] Miwoolies Creams.

197
00:07:49,550 --> 00:07:51,850
Dessert,
care of the First Capital.

198
00:07:51,890 --> 00:07:54,720
It's basically shaved ice atop
a mound of whipped cream,

199
00:07:54,770 --> 00:07:57,480
with some honey and nuts.
It is exquisite.

200
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,350
The bear is their mascot.

201
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:01,940
They are holding
a contest to name it.

202
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:03,900
[exclaims] Truly magnificent!

203
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:05,900
A testament
to cultural advancement!

204
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:07,900
Never heard of it.

205
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,530
But you have?

206
00:08:09,570 --> 00:08:12,870
Is it that shocking?
Everybody enjoys iced treats.

207
00:08:12,910 --> 00:08:14,410
♪

208
00:08:15,410 --> 00:08:18,370
Out with it.
What's that look about?

209
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:19,670
[TEORITTA] Speak, my knight!

210
00:08:19,710 --> 00:08:21,580
They look delectable,
do they not?

211
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,500
It would be a pity
to pass them by.

212
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:24,710
You cannot hide it.

213
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:27,010
You clearly wish to try one!

214
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,840
[sighs] All right, you win.

215
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,430
Grab the two that look best.

216
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:34,060
Do you want one?

217
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,850
I'll have to pass this time.

218
00:08:37,890 --> 00:08:39,980
I've been trying
to save up my scrip.

219
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:42,730
Just two. Use this.

220
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,400
Go ahead.

221
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,030
[TEORITTA] It shall be done.

222
00:08:46,070 --> 00:08:49,030
You have placed this task
in able hands! [chuckles]

223
00:08:55,530 --> 00:08:57,000
Xylo,

224
00:08:57,040 --> 00:09:00,000
you've given me reason
to reevaluate my opinion of you.

225
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:01,080
Huh?

226
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:03,920
You saved them.

227
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,420
My doomed knights
at Couveunge.

228
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,170
And at Zewan Gan,

229
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:10,220
you risked it all
to save those

230
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:11,800
who were prepared to abandon.

231
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:14,350
The people you saved
were grateful,

232
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:16,760
and won't soon forget you.

233
00:09:16,810 --> 00:09:18,310
Good to know.

234
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,900
Guess it wasn't all for nothing.

235
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:26,690
Before today, I didn't realize
you could smile.

236
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:28,110
[chuckles]

237
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:31,070
I'm usually too pissed off
to muster a stupid grin.

238
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:32,410
Even so,

239
00:09:32,450 --> 00:09:35,700
you've more than
proven yourself a capable ally.

240
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:37,910
Beyond that,

241
00:09:37,950 --> 00:09:40,790
your pact
with Goddess Teoritta...

242
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:42,870
I believe it may have saved her.

243
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,540
I don't follow.

244
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:47,800
Her story is rather unusual.

245
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:50,630
She was discovered
in the northern ruins.

246
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:52,800
After her excavation,

247
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:55,300
we of the 13th Order
of Holy Knights,

248
00:09:55,350 --> 00:09:56,890
assigned to pact with her,

249
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:59,520
were dispatched
to oversee the operation.

250
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:02,520
But a rift formed between
the military and Temple.

251
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,440
[laughs] That's a crying shame.

252
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,940
You dare laugh?

253
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,480
When you caused it
by killing goddess Senereva?

254
00:10:08,530 --> 00:10:09,650
Say what?

255
00:10:10,070 --> 00:10:11,650
[KIVIA] After what transpired,

256
00:10:11,690 --> 00:10:14,780
the military started
having ideas.

257
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:17,620
"If we're capable
of killing a goddess,

258
00:10:17,660 --> 00:10:21,120
perhaps we also have the power
to create more of them."

259
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,210
It was decided

260
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:27,920
the military would
use Teoritta for research.

261
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,500
[Xylo chuckles]

262
00:10:29,550 --> 00:10:33,670
Why bother calling it research?
They really meant "dissection."

263
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,840
True.

264
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,260
The temple opposed the notion,

265
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:40,220
but the military won out
in the end.

266
00:10:40,770 --> 00:10:44,100
However, that situation
has started to change.

267
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,480
In a short span of time,

268
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,900
your unit has taken out
two Demon Lords,

269
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:51,490
thus, proving the usefulness
of Goddess Teoritta.

270
00:10:51,530 --> 00:10:53,490
What do you mean
her "usefulness"?

271
00:10:53,530 --> 00:10:56,530
Are you saying they thought
she was useless before that?

272
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:59,370
How would they even know
when they had just found her?

273
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:02,790
We knew she possessed
the power to summon swords.

274
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:05,460
It was inscribed in the ruins
where she was found.

275
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:06,460
[Xylo grunts]

276
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:07,750
♪

277
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:09,880
[KIVIA] It is said
the goddesses came to us

278
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:12,260
during the First War
of Subjugation,

279
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:15,380
in what is known
as the Great Civilized Era.

280
00:11:15,590 --> 00:11:18,470
The goddesses serve
as a "gate" of sorts,

281
00:11:18,510 --> 00:11:22,140
and each one,
possesses a different nature.

282
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:25,100
One creates
various poisons.

283
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:28,020
One calls down lightning
and raging storms.

284
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:30,480
One foresees the future.

285
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:34,280
They awaken in response
to Demon Blights.

286
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:36,200
When their task is fulfilled,

287
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:39,240
they return to their coffins
to slumber.

288
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:43,830
I'm already well-informed
about the goddesses' power.

289
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:45,460
There's even a rumor

290
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:47,500
that one of them
brought Tatsuya here

291
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:48,880
from another world.

292
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:51,710
It was judged that the ability
to summon swords

293
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:52,920
wasn't good enough.

294
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,800
That it was far weaker
than the abilities

295
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,920
of the 12 other goddesses.

296
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:00,430
We knew that. Knew her fate.

297
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:03,350
Yet despite that,
we were still complicit.

298
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:06,890
Oh, I see.

299
00:12:06,930 --> 00:12:08,560
That explains a lot.

300
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:11,400
So your suicidal plan
in Couveunge

301
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:13,940
was just a sorry attempt
to atone for your sins.

302
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:15,530
[Kivia grunts]

303
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:17,990
[XYLO] It's despicable,

304
00:12:18,030 --> 00:12:20,570
even if she was
a useless goddess.

305
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:22,410
Here, please enjoy!

306
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,160
You have my gratitude!

307
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:28,290
Xylo, mission accomplished!
I purchased one for Kivia, too!

308
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,370
[Kivia gasps]

309
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:32,090
[Teoritta chuckles]

310
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:33,630
Come, you two, let us...

311
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:35,880
[exclaims] Hey!

312
00:12:36,090 --> 00:12:37,220
[sighs]

313
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:38,300
[groans]

314
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:41,510
Tell me about our next mission.

315
00:12:41,550 --> 00:12:42,470
Why now?

316
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:44,390
If we keep doing a good job,

317
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:46,680
she's less likely
to get dissected, right?

318
00:12:46,730 --> 00:12:47,850
[Kivia gasps]

319
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:51,150
Not sure what their
definition of "usefulness" is,

320
00:12:51,190 --> 00:12:53,940
but I'll make those
Galtuile bastards choke on it.

321
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,530
[KIVIA] Hm.

322
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:59,280
Defense.

323
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:03,120
That's why
your hero unit is here.

324
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:05,540
You'll defend this fortress
by yourselves...

325
00:13:06,290 --> 00:13:07,790
To the death.

326
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:11,870
To the death? Really?

327
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,290
That's right.

328
00:13:13,330 --> 00:13:15,550
You will defend the fortress
from the Demon Blight

329
00:13:15,590 --> 00:13:18,090
without backup
until the bitter end.

330
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:20,550
So it's a literal
suicide mission.

331
00:13:20,590 --> 00:13:23,010
Hey, Xylo, I need you
to keep your cool.

332
00:13:23,050 --> 00:13:24,720
Don't snap
and beat anyone to death--

333
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:26,970
What the hell kind of animal
do you think I am?

334
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:30,310
[VENETIM] Pardon me,
could you perhaps tell us more?

335
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:32,600
Such as the fine details
of this strategy?

336
00:13:32,650 --> 00:13:33,900
[commander snorts]

337
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:35,900
[COMMANDER] You'll stay here
at the fortress.

338
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,020
That is all.

339
00:13:37,070 --> 00:13:38,690
A war of attrition, then.

340
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:40,860
And how long
do you need us to hold out?

341
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:42,360
Until you die.

342
00:13:42,410 --> 00:13:44,120
-[Xylo grunts]
-Oh.

343
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,530
That's the plan.

344
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:47,660
The Ninth and Thirteenth Orders
will be at the rear,

345
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,660
watching and conserving
their strength.

346
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:52,040
Once you're all dead
and the fortress has been taken,

347
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:55,210
that will be their cue
to unleash a special attack.

348
00:13:55,590 --> 00:13:57,590
And what exactly might that be?

349
00:13:57,630 --> 00:13:59,130
It's poison.

350
00:13:59,170 --> 00:14:02,760
The ninth goddess will perform
a miracle for all to see.

351
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,090
[Xylo scoffs]

352
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:06,180
[XYLO] You think that will
kill the Demon Lord?

353
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:08,770
I hear you've been throwing
everything you have at it,

354
00:14:08,810 --> 00:14:11,480
yet you still haven't managed
to defeat it.

355
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,270
That is accurate.

356
00:14:13,690 --> 00:14:16,190
Our last plan
involved an ace sniper.

357
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:18,820
He delivered
the goddess' poison directly.

358
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:20,900
His efforts merely
induced a torpor

359
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,860
the beast easily
recovered from.

360
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,910
Even someone like Tsav
wasn't able to take it down?

361
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:27,910
Between that humbling outcome

362
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:30,240
and a vision of the future
from the third goddess,

363
00:14:30,290 --> 00:14:32,960
Galtuile decided
to revise the plan.

364
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,960
That was the birth
of our strategy

365
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,380
to set a massive trap
in Mureed Fortress.

366
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:38,920
It ends here.

367
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:41,210
We'll poison the Demon Lord
until it's dead.

368
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:43,720
So the idea is to
effectively cancel out

369
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:45,470
its ability to regenerate?

370
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:47,010
Meanwhile, we're to wait around

371
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:48,680
and buy you some time
until we die?

372
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,140
[COMMANDER] That is correct.

373
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,730
May Mureed Fortress become
the eternal resting ground

374
00:14:52,770 --> 00:14:55,310
for Demon Blight
Number 15, "Iblis."

375
00:14:55,350 --> 00:14:57,440
[VENETIM] I have a question,
Commander.

376
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:59,770
Is there any reason
we can't leave?

377
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,690
I mean, after luring
the Demon Lord

378
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:03,110
into the trap, of course.

379
00:15:03,150 --> 00:15:05,950
The reason is that
those are Galtuile's orders.

380
00:15:05,990 --> 00:15:09,120
If any of you attempt to leave
the fortress prematurely,

381
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:10,540
the sacred seals
on your necks

382
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:12,750
will kill the entire unit
instantly.

383
00:15:12,790 --> 00:15:15,160
[gasps] The entire unit?

384
00:15:15,210 --> 00:15:16,170
Well, then.

385
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:17,830
Is that necessary?

386
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,710
Or is there some
compelling reason

387
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:20,880
you want us dead?

388
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:25,720
[gasps]

389
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:30,390
[scoffs] So their hatred
demands our suffering.

390
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,680
Understood.
We'll carry out the plan.

391
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:34,350
-[gasps]
-[VENETIM] That said,

392
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:36,350
I'd like to propose
a few revisions,

393
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:37,400
if you don't mind.

394
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,610
Like what?

395
00:15:38,650 --> 00:15:39,770
[VENETIM] Simple.

396
00:15:39,810 --> 00:15:42,530
That pesky caveat
that we all blow up

397
00:15:42,570 --> 00:15:44,490
even if one of us
leaves the fortress...

398
00:15:44,530 --> 00:15:46,450
It's highly counterproductive.

399
00:15:46,490 --> 00:15:47,530
How so?

400
00:15:47,570 --> 00:15:49,700
I'm sure I don't need
to remind you

401
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,080
that we're
antisocial criminal miscreants,

402
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,910
so it's a forgone conclusion
that at least one of our ranks

403
00:15:54,950 --> 00:15:58,540
will try to save his own skin,
making success impossible.

404
00:15:58,580 --> 00:15:59,960
Here's a thought.

405
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,380
Kill us if we all leave,

406
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:05,170
or one bad apple will inevitably
spoil the whole mission.

407
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:07,720
That tiny change
would substantially increase

408
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,340
our chances of success.

409
00:16:09,390 --> 00:16:12,930
Oh, one more thing,
regarding Goddess Teoritta...

410
00:16:13,350 --> 00:16:15,060
Our goddess is kind.

411
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:17,940
The most compassionate soul
I've ever encountered.

412
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:21,400
Even if ordered to leave,
she'll wish to stay by our side.

413
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:23,360
I request that that be allowed.

414
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:24,570
Ha!

415
00:16:24,610 --> 00:16:26,530
I don't have the authority
to approve it.

416
00:16:26,570 --> 00:16:27,990
That's not my call to make.

417
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:30,070
The goddess is under
the jurisdiction of the 13--

418
00:16:30,110 --> 00:16:32,410
Hey, Xylo,
go and request permission

419
00:16:32,450 --> 00:16:33,990
from Captain Kivia.

420
00:16:34,030 --> 00:16:35,330
On it.

421
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,920
What else do you want me
to get for us?

422
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:43,250
We're going to need
more soldiers.

423
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:45,380
Understood. What else?

424
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:46,800
Weapons and provisions.

425
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:48,680
Isn't there anything else
you want?

426
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:50,550
-A pardon.
-[VENETIM] Understood.

427
00:16:50,590 --> 00:16:53,390
-What else?
-[Xylo sighs, grunts]

428
00:16:53,430 --> 00:16:55,100
[XYLO] Forget the pardon.

429
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:57,770
I want cavalry
and some artillery.

430
00:16:57,810 --> 00:17:00,100
Can you get Jayce
and Rhyno back?

431
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:02,810
[VENETIM] I'm afraid they're
still on the western front.

432
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:05,690
We might be able
to get Tsav back, though.

433
00:17:05,730 --> 00:17:07,150
Tsav, huh?

434
00:17:07,190 --> 00:17:09,610
[COMMANDER] Hey, what are you
discussing over there?

435
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:10,780
[VENETIM] Listen, Xylo.

436
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:12,950
That's not where
Captain Kivia's room is,

437
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:14,370
so don't waste your time.

438
00:17:14,410 --> 00:17:15,580
[XYLO] Oh, right.

439
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:16,790
[VENETIM] Go on.

440
00:17:16,830 --> 00:17:18,830
I'll make sure everything
is handled here.

441
00:17:18,870 --> 00:17:20,330
Just trust me and relax.

442
00:17:20,370 --> 00:17:22,250
[XYLO] I know you
too well to trust you.

443
00:17:22,290 --> 00:17:24,590
Can you really pull it off?

444
00:17:24,630 --> 00:17:26,460
Funny you should ask.

445
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:29,510
Though I highly doubt
you'll take me at my word.

446
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:31,430
Despite how I look,

447
00:17:31,930 --> 00:17:34,260
you should know,
there was a time

448
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:35,890
when yours truly
was on the verge

449
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:37,770
of saving the whole world.

450
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:45,770
I must say,
this is rather dreary.

451
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:48,320
I take it this means
I'm not being granted

452
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:49,610
a proper trial?

453
00:17:49,650 --> 00:17:52,990
A thousand pardons,
Venetim Leopool.

454
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:56,580
I would have preferred to speak
in a slightly nicer location.

455
00:17:56,910 --> 00:17:59,750
Honestly, I was hoping
our paths would cross.

456
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:01,830
I have a great deal
of respect for you.

457
00:18:01,870 --> 00:18:03,170
That so?

458
00:18:03,210 --> 00:18:06,040
Do you hope to pursue
a career as a con man too?

459
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,670
If that's the case,

460
00:18:07,710 --> 00:18:10,460
I really don't see why you would
admire someone like me,

461
00:18:10,510 --> 00:18:12,300
seeing as how I got
caught and all.

462
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:15,850
Right you are.
I completely agree with you.

463
00:18:15,890 --> 00:18:18,220
[VENETIM] Regarding the crime
I'm being charged with,

464
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:20,770
I suppose attempting
to sell off the royal palace

465
00:18:20,810 --> 00:18:23,390
to the circus
was a bridge too far?

466
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:26,940
True. You elevated fraud
to a whole new level.

467
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:29,780
Fabricating a mad story
about the entire capital

468
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:31,900
being relocated
in order to sell the land

469
00:18:31,950 --> 00:18:34,360
to a circus performing
in the area.

470
00:18:34,410 --> 00:18:35,990
Quite the talent.

471
00:18:36,030 --> 00:18:38,700
I intended to take
the advance payment and leave,

472
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:40,700
but things got out of hand.

473
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,540
There's investment fraud
not to mention

474
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:45,880
forgery
and counterfeiting to boot.

475
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,880
I have at least
a hundred complaints here

476
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,960
from the Verkle Development
Corporation.

477
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,590
[VENETIM] I'm so sorry.
Truly, I am.

478
00:18:52,630 --> 00:18:54,590
Spare me your apologies.

479
00:18:54,630 --> 00:18:56,010
Tell me,

480
00:18:56,050 --> 00:18:59,560
what first inspired your choice
to become a con man?

481
00:18:59,890 --> 00:19:01,220
[VENETIM] Good question.

482
00:19:01,270 --> 00:19:03,600
It's hard to say,
I guess I've always hated

483
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:05,600
seeing people look disappointed.

484
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:08,730
So I'd lie my way out
of any tough situation,

485
00:19:08,770 --> 00:19:11,190
then do the work
to make the lie consistent.

486
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:13,690
I can't imagine how much effort
that must have entailed,

487
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:15,240
and it's impressive
that you managed

488
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:18,370
to keep such a large-scale
operation equally consistent.

489
00:19:18,410 --> 00:19:20,160
[VENETIM] Thank you.

490
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,490
So, um,

491
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:24,330
should I be bracing myself
for the death penalty?

492
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:27,130
Actually,
your fate is far worse.

493
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:29,090
We have no intention
of punishing you

494
00:19:29,130 --> 00:19:31,130
for the fraud
or any of your other crimes.

495
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:33,420
So it's not the fraud?
Then, why--

496
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:35,470
[KAFZEN]
This is the true culprit.

497
00:19:35,930 --> 00:19:38,430
[VENETIM] You mean that
third-rate gossip rag

498
00:19:38,470 --> 00:19:41,100
I used to write drivel for?
What about it?

499
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:43,850
[KAFZEN] There's
a certain article you wrote.

500
00:19:43,890 --> 00:19:46,310
Spies controlled
by the Demon Blight,

501
00:19:46,350 --> 00:19:48,270
and masquerading as humans.

502
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:50,900
You boldly assert that
they've infiltrated the Temple,

503
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:54,940
as well as Galtuile
and even the royal family.

504
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:57,530
Right, they were
out of goddess scandals,

505
00:19:57,570 --> 00:20:00,120
as well as those
about the Holy Knights,

506
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:02,490
and even the stuff
about the royal family.

507
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:03,580
To drive sales,

508
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:05,080
they told me
they wanted an article

509
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:07,330
that would inspire fear
in the populace.

510
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:10,250
[KAFZEN] Well,
to be completely frank,

511
00:20:10,290 --> 00:20:11,920
fraud isn't a problem,

512
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:15,760
or forgery, inflated scandals,
conspiracy theories.

513
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,760
Those are all fine.

514
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,430
That said,

515
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:23,350
we can't have you going around
telling the truth.

516
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:24,430
[VENETIM] Huh?

517
00:20:24,470 --> 00:20:26,140
You have a particular talent

518
00:20:26,180 --> 00:20:27,690
for being able
to convince people

519
00:20:27,730 --> 00:20:29,600
of the most outrageous things.

520
00:20:29,650 --> 00:20:31,650
You're at least skilled enough
to make us believe

521
00:20:31,690 --> 00:20:33,900
you can achieve anything
with your words.

522
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:35,940
Wait, this is a huge mistake.

523
00:20:35,990 --> 00:20:37,320
Just give me a second
and I'll explain--

524
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:40,570
To prevent you from
speaking truth in the future,

525
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:42,950
we're going to be including
a special feature

526
00:20:42,990 --> 00:20:44,370
in your sacred seal.

527
00:20:46,330 --> 00:20:48,710
What? Please, no! [grunts]

528
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:50,830
-Stop! Just wait a minute!
-I'm afraid the death penalty

529
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:53,250
is too good
for someone like you.

530
00:20:53,290 --> 00:20:54,500
[VENETIM] You...

531
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:58,800
You can't. I swear,
I don't know anything!

532
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,380
I just...

533
00:21:00,430 --> 00:21:02,850
didn't want
to disappoint anyone.

534
00:21:02,890 --> 00:21:04,300
[Kafzen chuckles]

535
00:21:04,350 --> 00:21:06,640
Venetim Leopool.

536
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:10,020
-You are hereby sentenced...
-[Venetim whimpers]

537
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:12,150
...to be a hero.

538
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:18,820
[XYLO] I can't believe he got us
everything I asked for,

539
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:19,990
except the pardon.

540
00:21:20,030 --> 00:21:21,950
[DOTTA]
If the goddess is in danger,

541
00:21:21,990 --> 00:21:24,660
I'd bet good scrip that
Venetim will conjure up some way

542
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:25,910
to get her out of it.

543
00:21:25,950 --> 00:21:27,620
He's the cleverest guy I know.

544
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:30,370
Some way,
he's guaranteed to wind up

545
00:21:30,410 --> 00:21:32,040
with a knife in his back.

546
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:33,880
Speaking of,

547
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:36,290
do you think that Tsav
has already arrived?

548
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:38,010
Probably.

549
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:39,970
[sighs]

550
00:21:40,010 --> 00:21:43,260
Somehow, that guy found a way
to be even worse than Venetim.

551
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:44,430
You know...

552
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:47,010
Tsav is just so volatile
all the time.

553
00:21:47,060 --> 00:21:49,230
-[indistinct chatter]
-[MAN 1] He did it again!

554
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:51,560
[MAN 2] That man is unstoppable!

555
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,150
[MAN 3] Seven times in a row!

556
00:21:53,190 --> 00:21:54,690
[man 4 grunts]

557
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:57,320
[all exclaiming]

558
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:59,320
[MAN 5]
Yet another winning roll!

559
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:00,320
[laughs]

560
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:02,200
Looks like the pot's all mine!

561
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:05,160
Go on. It's time to pony up
my hard-earned scrip!

562
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:08,120
You should know, I can see
right through your little ploy.

563
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:09,290
Huh?

564
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:10,910
Somethin' you wanna say?

565
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,370
Actually, there is.

566
00:22:12,410 --> 00:22:14,960
I happen to have
keen eyes and ears.

567
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,460
Also,
I'm a brutally stand-up guy

568
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:20,420
who just hates to see
wrongdoers go unpunished.

569
00:22:20,710 --> 00:22:23,430
But if you give up the scrip
and leave, I won't have

570
00:22:23,470 --> 00:22:25,550
-to teach you a lesson--
-[MAN 6] You bastard!

571
00:22:25,590 --> 00:22:27,180
You'd better shut your mouth!

572
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:28,560
Take back those damn lies

573
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:29,680
-or else I'm gonna...
-[sword whooshes]

574
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:33,730
[whimpering]

575
00:22:35,650 --> 00:22:38,020
-[TSAV] We all saw that, right?
-[all gasping]

576
00:22:38,610 --> 00:22:41,440
Relieved the naughty fraudster
of his swindling hand.

577
00:22:41,490 --> 00:22:43,110
[screaming]

578
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:45,910
It's your own fault.

579
00:22:45,950 --> 00:22:48,160
I tried to warn you in advance.

580
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,370
[screaming continues]

581
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:51,080
[TSAV] But anyway...

582
00:22:51,790 --> 00:22:53,540
[Tsav grunts]

583
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:56,040
[Tsav sighs]

584
00:22:56,880 --> 00:22:59,000
I think it's dinner time.

585
00:23:00,750 --> 00:23:02,720
[♪ closing theme song playing]

